 "script": "New York's A I law gives big labs seventy-two hours to report a critical safety incident. The state opened a sign-up portal Tuesday, TechCrunch reported. Companies with over five hundred million dollars in revenue must register by January first. That includes OpenAI and Anthropic. Here's what changes in January. Big labs must publish their safety plans. Fines can reach one million dollars, or three million for repeat violations. California allows fifteen days to report. New York allows three. Governor Kathy Hochul said New York won't simply take A I companies at their word. Who should check A I safety claims? Tell us below.",
